 "notes": "Measurement paper: no PRF claim is made (creep resistance in the tetrahedron is not argued), so the spine ends at MEC -> DSC/conclusion. Two branches: primary (misfit reversal -> gamma' shearing, p20) and tertiary (load transfer -> p14, rafting p23). p4 DES/method kept off-spine although the in-situ phase-resolved measurement is close to a headline method. Audit p25 (text-silent in packet): the two nominally identical 650 C tests give different gamma' strain sign and misfit-reversal strain (F7a/b, F8a/b), which weakens the primary-creep identification. Audit on F5: residuals are worst for the separated high-intensity doublets, not for the overlapping case the text flags. Load partition between phases is typed MEC/pathway (mechanism_class=load partitioning), not PRP/partition, because it explains a regime rather than decomposing a property total. F3, F6 not opened."
}